    // A pivot-view search reads two kinds of names: source columns (they filter
    // the transactions, then the pivot is rebuilt from what is left) and
    // aggregate labels (they keep pivot rows by their cells). When a label and
    // a source column share a name - ?id=sponawd's "Amount" label on the AMOUNT
    // column, or a default "Count" label on a COUNT column - the AGGREGATE wins:
    // what is on screen is what is searched. A leading __SRC hands every shared
    // name back to its column; labels no column shares stay aggregates either
