    // ===== CHART THIS PIVOT (2026-08-27) ====================================
    // "Chart This Pivot" does NOT draw its own chart - it opens the real
    // Visualization Builder with the pivot's shape already filled in, so the
    // chart lands in the builder's preview with every one of its options (and
    // its Save-as-vis() path) available. Implementation is deliberately thin:
    // derive a viz config, park it in lastVisConfig, and let #visualizeBtn's
    // existing open sequence do the rest - script loading, column population,
    // restoreVizConfig() and the live preview.
    //
    // The builder plots RAW report rows: its X axis is a column dropdown and it
    // re-aggregates itself. So a pivot that buckets or re-shapes its rows
    // (bins, date splits, nested rows) or uses an aggregation the builder does
    // not have cannot be reproduced exactly - those are reported to the user
    // rather than silently charted as something else.
