        // Stop would stay hidden for every later query. Restoring it at the START
        // of each load makes that unrecoverable state impossible.
        penumbraClearBigRenderNotice();
        // A view change started from a layout_switch / toggle_switch, or a load
        // that only rearranges the data (opts.scoped), veils only the data
        // (_pnbLoadingScope); every other load keeps the full screen. A load
        // that starts while a veil is already up keeps it unless its caller says
        // otherwise: a big sort runs the formatting pass, which opens its own
        // "Applying custom formatting rules..." - measured live on dr-huron2
        // (7,104 rows), the one sort flipped from the veil to the full screen.
        try {
