    // Keys are compared as STRINGS, deliberately. Stored keys are always strings
    // (String(srv.ID) / String(snap.timestamp)), but callers that read the key off
    // the DOM with jQuery's .data('snap-key') get a NUMBER back - jQuery coerces
    // any numeric-looking data-* attribute ("1234" -> 1234). A strict === between
    // those two silently returned null, so the drawer's server-snapshot buttons
    // did nothing at all: no error, no toast, just an early return. (The callers
    // that pass sel[0].key already hold the stored string, so String() is a no-op
    // for them.) Use .attr() or String()-compare if you ever match keys elsewhere.
    function _findUnifiedSnap(kind, key) {
