     *
     * The manual email path builds its body HERE, in the browser, and POSTs an
     * opaque blob - share.php can only weigh the assembled message and refuse,
     * which is why it says so in its own comments. The scheduled path generates
     * server-side and truncates row by row instead. Same report, same recipient,
     * two different outcomes; this closes that gap by truncating at the only
     * place in the manual path where rows are still discrete objects.
